Role in KTAPEOUT: this is the pinned SilverScript compatibility layer used by the
Registry Adapter workbench to rebuild TN10 adapter contract scripts. The design
requires rebuilt parent and Gap scripts to match the deployed scripts byte for byte,
so this copy is pinned rather than tracking upstream. It is adapted to the pinned
rusty-kaspa revision used by this repository (01b532e8b553523216471682649693af92f0fd16)
and to Rust edition 2024. Changing it changes the compiler digest below and requires
re-running the byte-exact reconciliation against the recorded TN10 transactions.

Pinned digest of this directory (excluding LICENSE and NOTICE): 29 files,
SHA-256 c5b6e2ac6d2a52dbd0cd9b0b5ea9701c649787781438c656b3c37fd25b81f309. The digest is computed over the files sorted by UTF-8 relative path as
SHA-256 of the concatenation of: relative path, a NUL byte, the lowercase hexadecimal
SHA-256 of the file content, and a line feed.

Provenance gap: the exact upstream commit this copy was derived from was not recorded
when it was imported. Replacing this copy with a pinned upstream revision is possible
only after byte-exact reconciliation shows identical compiler output for the recorded
TN10 contracts.
